{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Call the initializer that wraps a throwing expression when you need to serialize","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or memoize the result.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Converting a Throwing Expression to a Result","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)"],"anchor":"Converting-a-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/swift-standard-library","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/preserving-the-results-of-a-throwing-expression","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes you need to preserve the entire result of a function call or other expression"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that can either throw or return a value. For example, you may need to serialize the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"result or pass it as a value to another part of your app that handles the result"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data. Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"},{"type":"text","text":" type in these scenarios to capture the result of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"potentially failing operation."}]},{"text":"Identify a Throwing Expression to Preserve","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Identify-a-Throwing-Expression-to-Preserve"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Typically, you use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do-catch"},{"text":" statements to handle throwing expressions immediately,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but sometimes you need to store the whole result of the operation for later processing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"during tasks like analyzing a batch of calls. The following example introduces an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API that generates random numbers, but that fails approximately half of the time.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum EntropyError: Error {","    case entropyDepleted","}","","struct UnreliableRandomGenerator {","    func random() throws -> Int {","        if Bool.random() {","            return Int.random(in: 1...100)","        } else {","            throw EntropyError.entropyDepleted","        }","    }","}"]},{"anchor":"Convert-the-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result","text":"Convert the Throwing Expression to a Result","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You preserve the return value or thrown error from a throwing expression using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"},{"text":" enumeration’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)"},{"text":" initializer. Invoke","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the throwing expression inside the closure you pass to the initializer:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let singleSample = Result { try UnreliableRandomGenerator().random() }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In most scenarios, you use the preserved result as part of broader functionality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in your code. For example, you may run a series of randomness tests and compute the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"statistical average of both a range of numbers returned from a random number generator,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as well as the failure rate of calling the API. In these cases, you need to store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole result rather than just the success value or that the API call failed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example uses the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)"},{"text":" initializer in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"broader context of saving a series of calls for later statistical analysis:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct RandomnessMonitor {","    let randomnessSource: UnreliableRandomGenerator","    var results: [Result<Int, Error>] = []","","    init(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator) {","        randomnessSource = generator","    }","","    mutating func sample() {","        let sample = Result { try randomnessSource.random() }","        results.append(sample)","    }","","    func summary() -> (Double, Double) {","        let totals = results.reduce((sum: 0, count: 0)) { total, sample in","            switch sample {","            case .success(let number):","                return (total.sum + number, total.count)","            case .failure:","                return (total.sum, total.count + 1)","            }","        }","","        return (","            average: Double(totals.sum) \/ Double(results.count - totals.count),","            failureRate: Double(totals.count) \/ Double(results.count)","        )","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Running the analysis on a sufficiently large sample generates an average number near","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"50 and a failure rate near 50%:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var monitor = RandomnessMonitor(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator())","(0..<1000).forEach { _ in monitor.sample() }","let (average, failureRate) = monitor.summary()","print(\"Average value: \\(average), failure rate: \\(failureRate * 100.0)%.\")","\/\/ Prints values such as: \"Average value: 47.95, failure rate: 48.69%.\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Preserving the Results of a Throwing Expression","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","references":{"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"type":"image","alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background.","identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]},{"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png","traits":["2x","dark"]}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/numbers-and-basic-values":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Numbers and Basic Values","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Model data with numbers, Boolean values, and other fundamental types.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Result":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value that represents either a success or a failure, including an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"associated value in each case."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/result","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Result","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Result","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/swift-standard-library":{"title":"Swift Standard Library","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/swift-standard-library","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Solve complex problems and write high-performance, readable code.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/swift-standard-library","type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","title":"Swift","kind":"symbol","images":[{"identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","type":"card"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Result/init(catching:)":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"catching","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultOsRi_zrlE7Failureq_mfp"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Success","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultOsRi_zrlE7Successxmfp"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/result\/init(catching:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new result by evaluating a throwing closure, capturing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned value as a success, or any thrown error as a failure."}],"title":"init(catching:)"}}}